      <description>Most Democrats running for California Governor say they’re steadfast in their decision to stay in the race. As Laura Fitzgerald, from our partners at CapRadio reports, that’s despite a plea from the Chair of California’s Democratic Party for low-polling candidates to drop out this week to avoid two Republicans making it to the November ballot.</description>
